title: "fluid-thermal-index: TEEI — Thermal Economic-Environmental Index"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-XX-XX"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Saination/fluid-thermal-index"
url: "https://Saination.github.io/fluid-thermal-index/"
abstract: >
  TEEI (Thermal Economic-Environmental Index) is a fluid-parameterised,
  multi-dimensional framework for comparing heating sources across economic,
  environmental, thermodynamic, and temporal dimensions. The package proves
  the cp-invariance theorem: TEEI source rankings are mathematically
  independent of which fluid is being heated.
keywords:
  - thermal economics
  - heat pump
  - specific heat capacity
  - levelized cost of heat
  - cp-invariance
  - TEEI
  - entropy generation
